# Repository

Drizzle only. `{Aggregate}Repository`. Speaks **entity**, not DTO. See [entity](./entity.mdc).

## Logic

- Persist / load. Missing row → `NotFoundError`. Failed write → `InternalServerError`.
- No policy (uniqueness, “may create if…”) — that is the use-case.

## Do

- `constructor(private readonly db: DbClient = defaultDb)`
- `find*` → entity via `Mapper.fromPersistence`
- `save(entity)` → `Mapper.toPersistence` then insert/update
- Transactions: `new UserRepository(tx)`; methods use `this.db`

## Don't

- `create(plain object)` while an entity exists
- Use-case rules, oRPC, other modules' repos
- `db` / `tx` on public method params

```ts
async findByEmail(email: string): Promise<User | null> {
  const [row] = await this.db.select().from(userTable).where(eq(userTable.email, email));
  return row ? UserMapper.fromPersistence(row) : null;
}

async save(user: User): Promise<void> {
  try {
    await this.db.insert(userTable).values(UserMapper.toPersistence(user));
  } catch (error) {
    throw new InternalServerError(ERROR_CODES.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, undefined, { cause: error });
  }
}
```
